From 38deb534cdc0cadf0aa6baa15728aa95cf7c4c79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:23:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-104: the properties panel's header as short as
 WPF's (0.104.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WPF's Properties window has the Name / type line, then the search box with
Arrange by beside it, then the grid. Here the header took six lines (name, the
tabs, the note, the path, a row of DFM 定義 / HTML 原始碼 / 複製名稱, the search,
a row of 排列 buttons). Now the three jump buttons are small ones at the end of
the tabs' line (DFM / HTML / 複製, the full meaning in their tooltips) and the
Arrange by buttons (類別 / 名稱 / DFM) sit beside the search box: the grid starts
two lines higher. README / CHEATSHEET say where they are now.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 187, panels, real VS Code 159):
panels (the Arrange by and tab checks unchanged, all pass); screenshot checked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
